{"content":[{"signature":"","thinking":"\nThe user is asking me to implement a `solve(case)` function for task AGENT-TF-01. Let me analyze what's needed:\n\n1. For each call, compute: `gain = loss_without_call - loss_with_call`\n2. Normalize the gain: `normalized_gain = gain / prediction_tokens`\n3. Accept a call if: `parseable == True` AND `normalized_gain \u003e= threshold`\n4. Return accepted_call_ids and diagnostics (in supplied call order)\n\nThe output schema requires:\n- `accepted_call_ids`: list of strings\n- `diagnostics`: list of objects with `accepted`, `call_id`, `normalized_gain`\n\nLet me verify with the first fixture case:\n- threshold: 0.05\n- call0: gain = 1.48911432 - 0.30132987 = 1.18778445, normalized = 1.18778445/5 = 0.23755689, parseable=true → accepted\n- call1: gain = 1.37006381 - 0.10127803 = 1.26878578, normalized = 1.26878578/5 = 0.25375716, parseable=true → accepted\n- call2: gain = 1.07992348 - 0.04054692 = 1.03937656, normalized = 1.03937656/5 = 0.20787531, parseable=true → accepted\n- call3: gain = 1.76582941 - 0.57732788 = 1.18850153, normalized = 1.18850153/3 = 0.39616718, parseable=true → accepted\n- call4: gain = 1.70674574 - 0.40289862 = 1.30384712, normalized = 1.30384712/6 = 0.21730785, parseable=true → accepted\n- call5: gain = 1.98682122 - 0.89260518 = 1.09421604, normalized = 1.09421604/4 = 0.27355401, parseable=false → rejected\n\nSo accepted: call0, call1, call2, call3, call4\n\nThe candidate artifact says \"rounded per-call diagnostics\" but doesn't specify rounding precision. I'll keep them as floats (Python's default float arithmetic should be fine).\n\nLet me write the implementation:\n\n```python\ndef solve(case):\n    threshold = case[\"threshold\"]\n    calls = case[\"calls\"]\n    \n    diagnostics = []\n    accepted_call_ids = []\n    \n    for call in calls:\n        call_id = call[\"call_id\"]\n        loss_without = call[\"loss_without_call\"]\n        loss_with = call[\"loss_with_call\"]\n        prediction_tokens = call[\"prediction_tokens\"]\n        parseable = call[\"parseable\"]\n        \n        gain = loss_without - loss_with\n        normalized_gain = gain / prediction_tokens\n        \n        accepted = parseable and normalized_gain \u003e= threshold\n        \n        diagnostics.append({\n            \"call_id\": call_id,\n            \"normalized_gain\": normalized_gain,\n            \"accepted\": accepted\n        })\n        \n        if accepted:\n            accepted_call_ids.append(call_id)\n    \n    return {\n        \"accepted_call_ids\": accepted_call_ids,\n        \"diagnostics\": diagnostics\n    }\n```\n\nThe \"rounded per-call diagnostics\" note - I'll leave normalized_gain as a float. The schema says `\"type\": \"number\"` which covers floats.\n\nNow I need to format this as a JSON response with a single key \"implementation\" containing the Python source as a JSON string.\n","type":"thinking"},{"text":"{\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    threshold = case[\\\"threshold\\\"]\\n    calls = case[\\\"calls\\\"]\\n\\n    diagnostics = []\\n    accepted_call_ids = []\\n\\n    for call in calls:\\n        call_id = call[\\\"call_id\\\"]\\n        loss_without = call[\\\"loss_without_call\\\"]\\n        loss_with = call[\\\"loss_with_call\\\"]\\n        prediction_tokens = call[\\\"prediction_tokens\\\"]\\n        parseable = call[\\\"parseable\\\"]\\n\\n        gain = loss_without - loss_with\\n        normalized_gain = gain / prediction_tokens\\n\\n        accepted = parseable and normalized_gain \u003e= threshold\\n\\n        diagnostics.append({\\n            \\\"call_id\\\": call_id,\\n            \\\"normalized_gain\\\": normalized_gain,\\n            \\\"accepted\\\": accepted\\n        })\\n\\n        if accepted:\\n            accepted_call_ids.append(call_id)\\n\\n    return {\\n        \\\"accepted_call_ids\\\": accepted_call_ids,\\n        \\\"diagnostics\\\": diagnostics\\n    }\\n\"}","type":"text"}],"id":"msg_01zhU0fLedubrSs6Tl